body:
Coordinator, merge note for head 7fe32c8d0c1f8f7687c2655a20734525fe4f475f. Class: no refresh (the head is the reviewed head).

This merge relies on:
- the review marker on this head (22:25Z, "Ready for the maintainer to merge");
- a trial merge here, on `main` ebc5cadd4 (the merge is clean and changes only the three files);
- a check with git that the change is a pure move: each line removed from `first_traverse.rs` is in `first_traverse_table.rs`. The only other lines are `pub(super)` on five moved items, the `use` lines and the provenance line of the new file, the `#[cfg(test)]` wrapper of the moved test, the re-export, and `mod first_traverse_table;`. `first_traverse.rs` goes from 432 to 320 lines; the new file has 131;
- 44 steps, 0 failed, 588 tests: the app lib (298), `conformance`, `golden_cl`, `posting`, each `first_traverse*`, `index_swing*`, `rotary*`, `tilt*`, `posed*` and `opening_rotary_pose` binary, and the three example catalog suites. Clippy on the `camcraft-app` lib is clean. No golden changed.

Not run: the other 620 app steps of the batch plan (the quick plan for this file is 321 steps), and `first_part_programs` (that test is red on `main` now for a different reason, #3572, and this PR does not change a post).

@FlamingFireCoding thank you for the split.
